<% title "FAQ" %>

<h1 class="heading">Frequently asked questions</h1>

<h2>What is Fuime?</h2>
<%# The previous version of this answer said an under-18 "cannot ... sign a contract
    on your own", which is not what the law says: a minor can sign, and the contract
    is voidable at the *minor's* option. That distinction is the whole reason the
    guardian structure exists, so the copy should teach it rather than flatten it. %>
<p>
  Fuime is a financial platform for businesses run by young founders. It keeps
  your books, stores your receipts, tracks what you might owe at tax time, and
  puts a parent or guardian on your venture as its legal signer.
</p>
<p>
  That last part is not red tape. Under 18, a contract you sign can be voided at
  your own option — which is why banks, payment processors, and suppliers will not
  rely on it, and why almost none of them will open an account for you. A
  guardian's signature is what makes your venture real to the people you do
  business with.
</p>

<h2>Does real money move through Fuime right now?</h2>
<% if StripeService.live? %>
  <p>
    Yes. Payments made to a business on Fuime are real.
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p>
    <strong>No.</strong> Fuime is in a pre-launch beta and everything runs
    against Stripe's test mode. Payment forms and cards work end to end so you
    can see how the product behaves, but no real money moves and a real card
    will not be charged. We will say so clearly, here and in the product,
    before that changes.
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2>Who can use Fuime?</h2>
<p>
  Anyone 13 or older. If you are under 18 you need a parent or legal guardian
  on your account before you can run a business. We do not accept anyone under
  13, and we ask you to confirm you are 13 or older when you sign up. We do not
  ask for your date of birth.
</p>

<h2>Why do I need a parent on the account?</h2>
<p>
  Because a minor cannot legally sign the agreements a business needs. Your
  parent or guardian is the adult who takes legal responsibility, which is what
  makes the whole thing work. They accept the
  <%= link_to "Guardian Agreement", guardian_agreement_path %>, and until they
  do, you cannot create a business.
</p>

<h2>What can my parent see?</h2>
<p>
  Everything about the businesses they sign for: transactions, balances,
  receipts, and who is on your team. This is not optional and you cannot turn
  it off. It is the deal that lets a teenager run a real business.
</p>

<h2>Can my parent change their mind?</h2>
<p>
  Yes, at any time. If they withdraw consent you can no longer operate a
  business on Fuime. Your records are not deleted automatically — see the
  <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path %>.
</p>

<h2>What does the tax tracker actually do?</h2>
<p>
  It watches your ledger and estimates whether you are approaching the IRS
  threshold where self-employment tax starts to apply. It is an
  <em>estimate</em> built from the records you enter — not a tax return, and
  not advice. Show it to an accountant before you rely on it. Tax rules also
  vary by state, and Fuime does not model that.
</p>

<h2>What does Fuime cost?</h2>
<p>
  Fuime keeps <%= Fuime::PaymentLinkService::FUIME_PLATFORM_FEE_PERCENT %>% of
  each payment processed for your business, shown as its own line on your
  ledger so you can always see it. There is no monthly fee. During the beta no
  real payments are processed, so nothing is charged.
</p>

<h2>Is Fuime a bank?</h2>
<p>
  No. Fuime is software for keeping records. It is not a bank, it does not hold
  deposits, and money tracked in Fuime is not FDIC-insured. See our
  <%= link_to "Terms of Service", terms_path %>.
</p>

<h2>What happens when I turn 18?</h2>
<p>
  The guardian requirement stops applying to you, and you can export your
  records to take to your own LLC or accountant. Ask us at
  <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %> and we will get you an export.
</p>

<h2>How do I get my data out, or delete it?</h2>
<p>
  Email <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %>. Export and deletion are not
  self-serve in the product yet, so we do them by hand. We do not charge for
  either. A parent can make the request too.
</p>

<h2>Something is broken. Who do I tell?</h2>
<p>
  <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %> for anything at all. For security
  vulnerabilities specifically, see our
  <%= link_to "security page", security_path %>.
</p>

<h2>Is Fuime open source?</h2>
<p>
  Yes. Fuime is a fork of
  <%= link_to "HCB", "https://github.com/hackclub/hcb", target: "_blank" %> by
  Hack Club — the platform that has handled fiscal sponsorship for teen
  nonprofits since 2018 — and is licensed under the AGPL-3.0. The source is at
  <%= link_to Rails.configuration.constants.github_url, Rails.configuration.constants.github_url, target: "_blank" %>.
</p>
